#compdef await

# Block on a job started by `async`, print its captured stdout and return
# its exit status: `await $id`.
#
# zshrs builtin. builtin_await (src/extensions/ext_builtins.rs) reads only
# argv[0] as a numeric job ID and takes no options. Job IDs are held in the
# shell's async table and are not exposed to shell code, so they cannot be
# listed here; keep in sync.
# Bundled into ~/.zshrs/functions by build.rs.

_arguments '1:async job ID (printed by async):'
